# Windows batch files (cmd.exe)

## CRLF is mandatory

`cmd.exe` mis-parses **LF-only** `.bat` / `.cmd` files. Typical symptom (German Windows):

```text
"." kann syntaktisch an dieser Stelle nicht verarbeitet werden.
```

`.gitattributes` already has `*.bat text eol=crlf` and `*.cmd text eol=crlf`, but editor/agent writes often land as LF on disk.

**After creating or editing any `.bat` / `.cmd`**, force CRLF before finishing:

```powershell
$path = "path\to\file.bat"
$text = [System.IO.File]::ReadAllText($path) -replace "`r`n", "`n" -replace "`n", "`r`n"
[System.IO.File]::WriteAllText($path, $text, [System.Text.UTF8Encoding]::new($false))
```

Verify with `git ls-files --eol -- file.bat` → working tree should show `w/crlf`.

## Never unescaped `(` `)` inside `( ... )` blocks

cmd treats parentheses as block syntax. An `echo ... (~80 MB)...` **inside** `if (...) (` breaks parsing. Symptom is often:

```text
"..." kann syntaktisch an dieser Stelle nicht verarbeitet werden.
```

```bat
REM BAD — paren inside a paren block
if not exist "%GODOT_EXE%" (
    echo downloading (~80 MB)...
)

REM GOOD — no parens in the echo, or escape them
if not exist "%GODOT_EXE%" (
    echo downloading ~80 MB...
    echo downloading ^(~80 MB^)...
)

REM ALSO GOOD — use goto labels instead of nested blocks for multi-line branches
```

Prefer `goto` labels for longer branches so echo text cannot break the parser.

## Never probe `.godot` from cmd

Do **not** use `if exist`, `dir`, or similar on paths that contain a **`.godot`** path segment. cmd can treat the `.` as a syntax error (same message as above).

```bat
REM BAD
dir /b "%ROOT%\.godot\imported" >nul 2>&1
if exist "%ROOT%\.godot\global_script_class_cache.cfg" goto launch
```

Use PowerShell instead — prefer the project helper:

```bat
REM GOOD
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "%ROOT%\tools\check_godot_import_artifacts.ps1" -InstallDir "%ROOT%" -Attempts 1 -DelayMs 0 >nul
if errorlevel 1 goto do_import
```

`project.godot` as a **filename** in `if exist` is usually fine; the trap is the **`.godot\` directory**.

## Style

- Prefer ASCII in REM/echo (avoid em-dashes / fancy quotes).
- Keep parentheses blocks simple; when unsure, `goto` labels instead of deep nesting.
